    {
      "name": "reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT214aloyNTRiSHBqZDNOWFRVaEhRelJhTFU5cWNHYxAB",
      "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 месяца назад",
      "rating": 5,
      "text": {
        "text": "During our vacation in Ulcinj, our three kids got food poisoning or some kind of stomach virus/bacteria after eating pizza at Sparta Beach Club. They suffered the worst vomiting and diarrhea I have ever seen, to the point that they were unable to control their bowels. My 10-year-old daughter was vomiting every hour, so we took her to the hospital.\nThe medical care was quick and excellent. The doctors and nurses were caring, kind, and very helpful. Because she was dehydrated, she was given IV fluids. We paid only 37 euros for the consultation.\nIt's also possible they caught a virus or bacteria from the sea. Ulcinj is a beautiful city, but it has a serious sewage problem. Wastewater is discharged into the Adriatic Sea.\nOn Teuta Boulevard, there is an open ditch filled with dirty, foul-smelling water, where you can clearly see pipes from nearby buildings discharging wastewater. That polluted water eventually flows into the sea.",
        "languageCode": "en"
      },
      "originalText": {
        "text": "During our vacation in Ulcinj, our three kids got food poisoning or some kind of stomach virus/bacteria after eating pizza at Sparta Beach Club. They suffered the worst vomiting and diarrhea I have ever seen, to the point that they were unable to control their bowels. My 10-year-old daughter was vomiting every hour, so we took her to the hospital.\nThe medical care was quick and excellent. The doctors and nurses were caring, kind, and very helpful. Because she was dehydrated, she was given IV fluids. We paid only 37 euros for the consultation.\nIt's also possible they caught a virus or bacteria from the sea. Ulcinj is a beautiful city, but it has a serious sewage problem. Wastewater is discharged into the Adriatic Sea.\nOn Teuta Boulevard, there is an open ditch filled with dirty, foul-smelling water, where you can clearly see pipes from nearby buildings discharging wastewater. That polluted water eventually flows into the sea.",
        "languageCode": "en"
      },
